{
  "name": "rust-antlr",
  "description": "rust-antlr provides an ANTLR4-based grammar specification for the Rust programming language, supporting both full program parsing and simplified token-tree representations for lexical validation. The repository includes specialized Unicode identifier definitions and a Racket-based testing suite designed to exercise the grammar against real-world Rust source files. Although the lexer-focused token-tree mode successfully validates delimiter matching, the comprehensive program parser demonstrates significant performance bottlenecks characteristic of complex LL(*) grammar definitions.",
